/E (Support vector machines have been effectively used to predict temperature and rainfall patterns \([Pal and Deswal, 2008]\), while random forests have been employed for downscaling climate data \([Bedia et al., 2013]\) and predicting extreme weather events. These models can capture non-linear relationships between climatic variables and are particularly effective when combined with feature selection and preprocessing techniques. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
